.TH RAG-BONE 1 "2026-09-15" "rag-bone 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rag-bone \- search documentation and source code locally
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rag-bone
.RI [ \-\-config " FILE" ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rag-bone
indexes documentation and multi-language source trees, then searches the
resulting local index using dense, BM25, or hybrid retrieval.
It supports human-readable output as well as JSON and compact output
intended for software agents.
.PP
Relative source paths and index paths are resolved from the directory that
contains the configuration file.  If no configuration file exists,
.B rag-bone
uses its built-in defaults.  Model files may be downloaded on first use and
are reused from a per-user cache.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B config
Print the effective configuration.  With
.BR \-\-init ,
write a default configuration without overwriting an existing file.
.TP
.B index
Index the configured source directories.  Existing content hashes make the
operation incremental unless
.B \-\-reindex
is specified.
.TP
.B search
Search the index for a natural-language query and print the most relevant
chunks.
.TP
.B search-batch
Read one nonempty query per line from standard input and emit one JSON
object per line.  Models remain loaded between queries.
.TP
.B watch
Watch source directories and update the index when files change.
.TP
.B eval
Evaluate a tab-separated golden set and report Recall, MRR, and latency.
.TP
.B get
Fetch an indexed chunk by the identifier returned by
.BR "search \-\-compact" .
This command does not load models.
.TP
.B outline
List the indexed chunks and structural metadata for a file, in source
order.  This command does not load models.
.TP
.B find
Find indexed definitions whose symbol matches the supplied name.  Exact
matches are shown before substring matches.  This command does not load
models.
.TP
.B catalog
List indexed document sets that originated from the web.  This command does
not load models.
.TP
.B status
Show index statistics, including the model, provider, file count, and chunk
count.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Read configuration from
.IR FILE .
The default is
.IR ./.rag-bone.toml .
.TP
.BR \-h , " " \-\-help
Display help.  Place this option after a command to display
command-specific help.
.TP
.BR \-V , " " \-\-version
Display version information.
.SS Index and watch options
.TP
.BI \-\-path " PATH"
Override the configured source directories.  For
.BR index ,
this option may be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-\-model " MODEL"
Override the configured embedding model for
.BR index .
.TP
.B \-\-reindex
Rebuild the index from scratch, ignoring cached content hashes.
.SS Search options
.TP
.BR \-k , " " \-\-limit " " N
Return at most
.I N
results.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Write a JSON array to standard output.  Available for
.BR search ,
.BR get ,
.BR outline ,
.BR find ,
and
.BR catalog .
.TP
.B \-\-compact
Return chunk identifiers and one-line previews instead of full snippets.
.TP
.B \-\-no-rerank
Disable cross-encoder reranking.
.TP
.BI \-\-reranker " RERANKER"
Override the configured reranker with a registry identifier, model name, or
path to an ONNX file.
.TP
.BI \-\-retrieval " MODE"
Select
.BR dense ,
.BR bm25 ,
or
.BR hybrid
retrieval.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " LIST"
Restrict results to a comma-separated list of languages, such as
.BR rust,md .
.TP
.BI \-\-path-prefix " TEXT"
Keep only results whose path contains
.IR TEXT .
.TP
.BI \-\-source " TEXT"
Keep only web-sourced results whose source URL contains
.IR TEXT .
Use
.B catalog
to inspect available sources.
.SS Other command options
.TP
.BI \-\-context-lines " N"
For
.BR get ,
include
.I N
source lines before and after the indexed span.
.TP
.BI \-\-queries " FILE"
For
.BR eval ,
read test cases from
.IR FILE .
The default is
.IR eval/queries.tsv .
.TP
.BI \-\-dump " FILE"
For
.BR eval ,
write per-query results as JSON Lines to
.IR FILE .
.TP
.BI \-k " N"
For
.BR eval ,
use
.I N
as the Recall cutoff and number of scored results.  The default is 3.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Sets the base directory for shared model and embedding caches.  If unset,
.B rag-bone
uses
.IR $HOME/.cache .
.TP
.B RAG_BONE_MODEL_CACHE
Overrides the directory used for downloaded model files.
.TP
.B HF_HOME
Overrides the Hugging Face cache location used by the model loader.
.TP
.B RAG_NO_EMB_CACHE
If set, disables the persistent embedding cache while indexing.
.TP
.B ORT_DYLIB_PATH
Overrides the ONNX Runtime shared library.  The Debian package wrapper
sets a package-local default automatically.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./.rag-bone.toml
Default project configuration file.
.TP
.I CONFIG-DIRECTORY/.rag-bone/index.bin
Persisted project index, stored beside the selected configuration file.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/rag-bone/
Shared models and embedding vectors.  Defaults to
.I $HOME/.cache/rag-bone/
when
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
is unset.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed successfully.
.TP
.B nonzero
The command failed, for example because configuration, index, model, or
input data could not be read or validated.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Create a configuration and index documentation and Rust sources:
.PP
.EX
rag-bone config \-\-init
rag-bone index \-\-path ./docs \-\-path ./src
.EE
.PP
Search and then retrieve one selected chunk with surrounding source lines:
.PP
.EX
rag-bone search \-\-compact "where is token validation implemented?"
rag-bone get 1\-CHUNK_ID \-\-context-lines 5
.EE
.PP
Process several queries without reloading the models:
.PP
.EX
printf '%s\en' "first query" "second query" | rag-bone search-batch
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR grep (1),
.BR find (1)
.PP
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/automataIA/rag-bone-rs
.UE
